# Dependencies (Maven)

## BOM

- Use Spring Boot BOM (parent or dependencyManagement import) for consistent versions; override only when necessary.
- Prefer managed versions; declare versions in one place (parent or BOM import).

## Scopes

- compile (default), runtime, test, provided; use test for JUnit, Mockito, WireMock; provided for Lombok, annotation processors.

## Security

- Run mvn dependency-check or OWASP plugin; fix or suppress with justification; keep dependencies updated.
- Prefer well-maintained libraries; check CVE and release notes.

## Licensing

- Only compatible licenses (MIT, Apache-2.0, etc.); no GPL in proprietary without legal review; document license of key deps.
- Use license-maven-plugin or similar to report.

## Conventions

- Minimal dependencies; BOM for versions; security scan in CI; no snapshot in release; lockfile or flatten for reproducible builds when needed.

## Anti-Patterns

- Duplicate or conflicting versions; unnecessary deps; ignoring CVEs; GPL in proprietary without approval

